   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to duties of the commissioner of health; and to amend the executive law, in relation to qualifications to serve as a volunteer emergency medical technician",
    "basePrintNo": "S5542",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5542-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3011, Pub Health L; add §837-s, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5542\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to duties of the\ncommissioner of health; and to amend the executive law, in relation to\nqualifications to serve as a volunteer emergency medical technician\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would require a prospective volunteer emergency medical tech-\nnician to authorize a background check for sex offense convictions if\nthe individual chooses to proceed with his or her application.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends section 3011 of the Public Health Law by adding a new\nsubdivision 12 which provides that the Commissioner of Health shall\nrequire any emergency medical technician application of a volunteer\nambulance company to subject him or herself to a background check pursu-\nant to section 837-s of the Executive Law.\n\nSection 2: Amends the Executive Law by adding a new section 837-s which\nprovides for background checks for emergency medical technician appli-\ncants to join volunteer ambulance companies.\n\nSection 3: Effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nVolunteer ambulance companies should have the ability to deny membership\nto anyone who is a registered sex offender. Emergency Medical Techni-\ncians are usually in situations where children and families are present\nand vulnerable due to a medical emergency. It is also common for ambu-\nlance companies to participate m community and school events in which\nchildren are present. This bill would allow the ambulance company to\nscreen prospective volunteers and authorizes the ambulance company to\ndetermine whether the applicant shall be eligible to become a member of\nsuch company.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect one hundred and twenty days after it shall\nhave become a law.\n\n",
